              "text": "The next NBA game is **Game 1 of the 2026 NBA Finals** between the **New York Knicks** and the **San Antonio Spurs**. The game will take place on **Wednesday, June 3, 2026**, at **7:30 PM local time (8:30 PM ET)** at the **Frost Bank Center** in San Antonio, Texas.\n\nGiven the historic nature of this matchup (a rematch of the 1999 NBA Finals and the Knicks' first Finals appearance in decades), tickets are in extremely high demand. \n\nHere is exactly where and how you can purchase tickets:\n\n### 1. Official Primary Marketplace\n* **Ticketmaster:** As the official ticketing partner of both the NBA and the San Antonio Spurs, **[Ticketmaster](https://www.ticketmaster.com)** is the most secure place to buy verified primary and resale tickets.\n* **\ud83d\udea8 Important Restriction:** To prevent opposing team fans from taking over the arena, the Spurs have implemented a **150-mile residency restriction** for ticket sales at the Frost Bank Center. Your billing zip code on your payment method must be within 150 miles of the arena to successfully complete a purchase through primary channels.\n\n### 2. Secondary/Resale Ticket Platforms\nIf you do not live within the 150-mile radius, or if the primary tickets are sold out, you can look to verified secondary resale platforms:\n* **StubHub**\n* **SeatGeek** \n* **TickPick**\n* **Vivid Seats**\n\n### What to Expect on Ticket Prices (as of late May 2026)\n* **Games 1 & 2 (San Antonio):** \"Get-in\" prices (cheapest nosebleed seats in the upper bowl) are starting at **over $1,000\u2013$1,300**. Lower bowl seats are climbing past **$2,000**, with premium courtside seats hitting anywhere from **$9,000 to $47,000**. \n* **Games 3 & 4 (New York at Madison Square Garden):** If you are looking to attend a game at \"The Mecca,\" be prepared for unprecedented pricing. Resale tickets for Games 3 and 4 are currently starting at **$3,700 to $4,200+** just to get through the door. \n\n*Tip: Always use official partner links and verified secondary marketplaces to avoid counterfeit tickets, and ensure you read the venue's entry and gear policies before heading to the arena.*",
